    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2020-october/q2",
      "question": "<p>In an Argand diagram, the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are represented by the complex numbers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-3+2\\mathrm i\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5-4\\mathrm i\"></span> respectively. The points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are the end points of a diameter of a circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the equation of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, giving your answer in the form<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"|z-a|=b\\qquad a\\in\\mathbb C,\\ b\\in\\mathbb R\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\"></span>, with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|z-2-3\\mathrm i|=2\"></span>, intersects <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at the points representing the complex numbers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_2\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Find the complex numbers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_2\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
