      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2020-october/q6",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M=\\begin{pmatrix}k&amp;5&amp;7\\\\1&amp;1&amp;1\\\\2&amp;1&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\\qquad\\text{where } k \\text{ is a constant}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\neq 4\"></span>, find, in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>, the inverse of the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Find, in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>, the coordinates of the point where the following planes intersect.<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}2x+5y+7z&amp;=1\\\\x+y+z&amp;=p\\\\2x+y-z&amp;=2\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> for which the following planes intersect in a straight line.<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}4x+5y+7z&amp;=1\\\\x+y+z&amp;=q\\\\2x+y-z&amp;=2\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></div></li><li>For this value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span>, determine a vector equation for the line of intersection. <span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li></ol></li></ol>",
